#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "CAP-RECORDS Records lifecycle and data-subject rights"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Every record has a retention class; archiving, disposal, subject access, rectification and individual disclosure follow declared, audited paths."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: governance · depends on: [CAP-CLASSIFICATION]{1}, [CAP-MASTERDATA]{2}, [CAP-AUDIT]{3}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Each record is kept as long as it's needed and no longer, and people can see and correct what's held about them."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "How long personal data about children is kept is set by law and by purpose, not by the cost of storage. A platform that is append-only, branched and backed up keeps copies everywhere unless disposal is designed in from the start. Scheduled disposal is also the one approved exception to [P12]{1}: real data is never dropped on a guess, but it is removed when its retention period ends."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "A retention schedule in code, for each record class."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "A read-only archive for records whose retention trigger has occurred."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Requests for subject access, rectification and individual disclosure, each of them logged."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Where history can't be rewritten, as with immutable snapshots and backups, encrypt each subject's or partition's data with its own key, and destroy the key at disposal. Set table-history retention, branch lifetimes and backup windows so that none of them lasts beyond the disposal deadline."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "CAP-RECORDS.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "A retention schedule in code gives each record class its retention period, trigger event, legal basis and owning role, and every table and file belongs to a record class.{1}*Example:* Record class 'attendance session': kept for a stated number of years after the academic period ends, under the education law, owned by the learners steward."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "A fitness function finds no table or file without a record class."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "CAP-RECORDS.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "When a record's retention trigger occurs, the record leaves operational use and moves to a read-only archive."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "A leaver fixture appears in the archive and is read-only."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "CAP-RECORDS.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Disposal at the end of retention is a reviewed, audited operation that reaches table history, branches and backups within a stated maximum time; where history cannot be rewritten, per-subject or per-partition keys are destroyed. This is the only path by which real personal data is deleted.{1}*Example:* When a record class reaches its disposal date, the rows are deleted from current tables, table history older than the stated maximum is expired, and the key protecting the backed-up copy is destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "A disposal fixture leaves no readable copy in any store within the stated time; the audit shows the review."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "CAP-RECORDS.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Any record class kept without limit is listed as such in the schedule, with the reason."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "The schedule lists the permanent classes explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "CAP-RECORDS.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "A subject-access request is answered from the catalog by the person's identifier across all domains, and the answer is reproducible.{1}*Example:* A guardian asks what is held about their child; one query by the learner's identifier returns enrolments, attendance, results and support plans from every domain."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Two runs of a subject-access fixture return identical results."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "CAP-RECORDS.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "A rectification is an evented correction that creates a new version, and downstream tables are rebuilt from it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "After a rectification fixture, gold reflects the corrected value and the history shows both."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "CAP-RECORDS.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "Releasing an individual's records to that person, a guardian with verified authority, or an authorised agency is a logged request that records who received what, why, on what basis and how; it is separate from statistical publication, which never releases individual records.{1}*Example:* A receiving institution asks for a transferring learner's records; the release is logged with the requester, the purpose 'continuity of education', the legal basis, the categories sent and the channel."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-records.md
msgid "The disclosure register has an entry for each release with all fields."
msgstr ""

